meta { title = Local modules, order = 6, group = Learn }

Use export to expose a declaration, and from with import to bring named exports into another file. The ./ prefix resolves relative to the importing source file.

h2 { Split a program }

Save these files in the same directory. main.kalandra imports double from math.kalandra. The project compiler follows the import, shares its exported type information, and emits both modules.

{{example:modules}}

codeblock { language = bash, "bun run cli run /path/to/main.kalandra --strict" }

h2 { Build without running }

The build command writes native JavaScript ESM and source maps without executing the source:

codeblock { language = bash, "bun run cli build /path/to/main.kalandra -o dist/my-program --strict" }

Build and run use the nearest enclosing kalandra.toml and its build.source when present. Standalone files use their containing directory as the source root. Module cycles remain unsupported.

Installed Kalandra packages under .kalandra/modules are supported. The install command explicitly installs Git dependencies from kalandra.toml and records commit locks. JavaScript imports use explicit esm: or cjs: prefixes; packages can supply Kalandra type declarations. Importing a package is separate from installing it.

These package features are available locally. The single-file playground intentionally does not fetch modules or packages.

